NAME
    false - exit with a failure status

SYNOPSIS
    false

DESCRIPTION
    Does nothing and always exits with status 1. Intended for use in
    conditional statements and loops such as 'until false; do ...; done'.

EXAMPLES
    false
    echo $?

EXIT STATUS
    1   Always fails.

SEE ALSO
    true(1), test(1), if(1), while(1)
